ral comments that are being prepared for future import to Neotoma.","recdatecreated":"2026-02-14T05:06:53"}]}},{"site":{"siteid":41992,"sitename":"Jäckelberg-Huk","sitedescription":"Site is situated on the northeastern edge of the Jäckelberg spit, at a depth of 8.5 m below sea level.","sitenotes":"Submarine excavation at a late Mesolithic site","geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[11.46196,54.05691]}","altitude":-8,"collectionunitid":55845,"collectionunit":"Poel 45","handle":"POEL45","unittype":"Section","datasets":[{"doi":[],"agerange":[],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":74548,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"S.","contactid":8711,"firstname":"Steffen","familyname":"Wolters","contactname":"Wolters, Steffen"}],"datasettype":"geochronologic","datasetnotes":null,"recdatecreated":"2026-06-09T14:22:43"},{"doi":["10.21233/npbw-vf39"],"agerange":[{"units":"Calibrated radiocarbon years BP","ageold":8034,"ageyoung":7506}],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":74549,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"S.","contactid":8711,"firstname":"Steffen","familyname":"Wolters","contactname":"Wolters, Steffen"}],"datasettype":"pollen","datasetnotes":null,"recdatecreated":"2026-06-09T14:22:52"}]}},{"site":{"siteid":42019,"sitename":"Lake Skaansø","sitedescription":"Skaansø is a small lake surrounded by conifer plantation with scattered oak and birch on fluvioglacial sand. Sediment distribution is strongly influenced by dominant northwestern winds.","sitenotes":null,"geography":"{\"type\":\"Polygon\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[[[8.82537,56.50698],[8.82537,56.5117],[8.83272,56.5117],[8.83272,56.50698],[8.82537,56.50698]]]}","altitude":8,"collectionunitid":55876,"collectionunit":"Skaanso A2","handle":"SKANSO-2","unittype":"Core","datasets":[{"doi":["10.21233/3feq-sa72"],"agerange":[{"units":"Calibrated radiocarbon years BP","ageold":6165.48,"ageyoung":-35},{"units":"Radiocarbon years BP","ageold":5469,"ageyoung":-35}],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":74584,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"B.V.","contactid":1181,"firstname":"Bent V.","familyname":"Odgaard","contactname":"Odgaard, Bent V."}],"datasettype":"pollen","datasetnotes":null,"recdatecreated":"2026-06-19T20:55:41"},{"doi":["10.21233/znf4-qs16"],"agerange":[{"units":"Calibrated radiocarbon years BP","ageold":6165.479492,"ageyoung":-35},{"units":"Radiocarbon years BP","ageold":5469,"ageyoung":-35}],"database":"Neotoma Charcoal Data","datasetid":75265,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"B.V.","contactid":1181,"firstname":"Bent V.","familyname":"Odgaard","contactname":"Odgaard, Bent V."}],"datasettype":"microcharcoal","datasetnotes":"Quantification of microscopic charred particles and dark-coloured hyphae in the pollen slides was done by a calibrated eyepiece graticule with a grid of 21 by 21 lines mounted in a 10X ocular and using a 24X objective.\r\nThis method of estimating microscopic charred particle frequencies is generally similar to the method developed independently by Clark (1982).\r\nThe charred particle concentrations are divided by the pollen concentrations of terrestrial taxa and are shown as area of microfossils per pollen (micrometer square/pollen concentration ).","recdatecreated":"2026-09-25T12:18:32"},{"doi":[],"agerange":[],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":74583,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"B.V.","contactid":1181,"firstname":"Bent V.","familyname":"Odgaard","contactname":"Odgaard, Bent V."}],"datasettype":"geochronologic","datasetnotes":null,"recdatecreated":"2026-06-19T20:55:31"}]}},{"site":{"siteid":42019,"sitename":"Lake Skaansø","sitedescription":"Skaansø is a small lake surrounded by conifer plantation with scattered oak and birch on fluvioglacial sand. Sediment distribution is strongly influenced by dominant northwestern winds.","sitenotes":null,"geography":"{\"type\":\"Polygon\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"prop